  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a3300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3308.03 Processed Wood Residue Fuel Quality",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3308.03 Processed Wood Residue Fuel Quality. A large MWC facility combusting PWR shall only combust PWR that contains:\n\n(a) No more than 1% by weight of non-wood materials, including but not limited to drywall, concrete, aggregates, dirt, and asbestos;\n\n(b) No more than 1.5% by weight of wood treated with creosote, pentachlorophenol, chromated copper arsenate, or other copper, chromium, or arsenical preservatives;\n\n(c) No more than 10% weight of #4 minus fines;\n\n(d) No more than a total of 50 parts per million (mg/kg) dry weight basis of arsenic; and\n\n(e) No more than a total of 250 parts per million (mg/kg) dry weight basis of lead.\n\nSource. #12628, eff 9-27-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a3300.html"
